---
Check all malloc/calloc return values for NULL.

Unchecked allocation failures cause NULL pointer dereference crashes.
Every allocation must be checked and handled gracefully.

## Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] Every malloc/calloc/realloc call checks for NULL return
- [ ] On allocation failure: log error, return error code or use fallback
- [ ] No crash when allocation fails (graceful degradation)

## Test Plan
- [ ] Audit all malloc/calloc/realloc calls in src/engine/ and src/formats/
- [ ] Verify each has a NULL check with appropriate error handling
- [ ] Optional: inject allocation failures with a test allocator
